# Nothing has asked about the mouse and the primary screen is the active one,
# so the wheel is the terminal's own. Four lines onto a grid of two leave two
# behind, and turning the wheel up is what walks the viewport back into them
# — the screen below is the proof, and the app holds no scroll position of
# its own.
out "one\x0d\x0atwo\x0d\x0athree\x0d\x0afour"
wheel 0 2 0 0
# Already at the top of the history. The engine clamps it, so nothing moves —
# and the wake count is what says that a turn which moved nothing published
# nothing.
wheel 0 5 0 0
